# =============================================================================
# Vera frontend environment variables
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values for development.
# Never commit `.env.local`. Production values live in Vercel project settings.
#
# CRITICAL: The placeholder values below (anything containing the literal
# string "placeholder", or the unfilled `pk_test_...` / `sk_test_...` stubs)
# are NOT valid Clerk keys. Production deploys with placeholder values will:
#   1. Surface a loud warning from `middleware.ts` on the first request.
#   2. Be rejected by `scripts/check-env.mjs` if you wire it into your CI
#      pipeline (recommended — see frontend/scripts/check-env.mjs).
#   3. Cause Clerk components on /login and /register to crash at runtime
#      (visible 500 errors, broken sign-in flow).
# Replace every `*_CLERK_*` placeholder with a real value from your Clerk
# dashboard at https://dashboard.clerk.com before deploying.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Clerk (human auth for the dashboard)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Publishable key — safe to expose to the browser bundle.
# Format: pk_test_<base64> for dev, pk_live_<base64> for production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_placeholder_replace_before_deploy

# Secret key — server-only. NEVER expose this to the client bundle.
# Format: sk_test_<base64> for dev, sk_live_<base64> for production.
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_placeholder_replace_before_deploy

# Optional: customize the Clerk URLs. Sensible defaults work, but Vera maps
# its existing /login and /register paths to Clerk's hosted components.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_IN_URL=/login
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_UP_URL=/register
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_AFTER_SIGN_IN_URL=/dashboard
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_AFTER_SIGN_UP_URL=/dashboard
